            <ArticleTitle>[Symptoms of depressive state in otolaryngology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A psychiatric study was carried out to seek correct diagnosis and effective therapy for patients with various pain symptoms in ear, nose and throat area, and the unknown cause of pain and invalid treatment. There were 12 patients who coincided with the diagnostic criteria of depression. The therapeutic effect was satisfactory with antidepression medicine. It is suggested that the practicing ENT doctors should have some knowledge of psychiatry, understand the symptoms of depressive state, avoid misdiagnosis and offer correct management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
